1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,700
Good evening, Sandow, and welcome to the October 5th meeting of the Board of Selectmen.

2
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,520
I called the meeting to order and we'll start off with the Pledge of Allegiance.

3
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:25,080
I pledge allegiance to the flag of the United States of America and to the republic for

4
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:30,780
which it stands, one nation, under God, and indivisible, with liberty and justice for all.

5
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:38,540
All right, in attendance tonight, we have our town administrator, Lynn Blaisdell, selectman

6
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,880
Eddie Mensis, I'm the chair, Eric Golsan, to my right is Megan Daly, the vice chair.

7
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,620
Ben and Tom are not here tonight, and...

8
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:47,580
Did you push the button?

9
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:48,900
Did you push the button?

10
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:49,420
Yes, I did.

11
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:50,320
Thank you so much.

12
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:54,660
And Secretary, Quentin Secretary, Beth Cashman is not here tonight, so...

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:59,060
We're going to start off with the review of the minutes from last week, which I'm sure

14
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:02,200
everybody had a chance to prove it since they were short and sweet.

15
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,640
Maybe Ray, I'll entertain a motion.

16
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:13,500
I'll make a motion to approve the minutes from September 28th, 2026.

17
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:14,620
We have a second.

18
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:15,940
Second by Eddie.

19
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:16,900
All those in favor say aye.

20
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:17,300
Aye.

21
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:19,100
You got non-public, correct?

22
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:19,560
Yep.

23
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,660
So we can do those two.

24
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:26,020
I'll make a motion to approve the non-public minutes from September 28th, 2026.

25
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:26,940
We have a second.

26
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,920
Megan, all those in favor say aye.

27
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:29,360
Aye.

28
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:29,660
Aye.

29
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:30,160
Okay.

30
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:31,180
Public comment.

31
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,600
So who would like to go first?

32
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:33,600
Now I can give it to you.

33
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,620
Linda, let you go first.

34
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:35,960
Thank you.

35
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:43,980
Name for the record.

36
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,800
Name and address and everything first?

37
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:46,780
Yeah, that's fine.

38
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,660
Linda Brown, 23 Hunt Pond Road.

39
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:52,180
Hi.

40
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,500
I didn't really prepare anything.

41
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:56,740
I just really did want to give a comment.

42
00:01:56,740 --> 00:02:01,160
I think we need to do a better job with signage for our elections.

43
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:04,500
I did talk to Tom about this during the primary.

44
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:12,680
I do a lot of driving with my work, and I drove around to different towns, and a lot

45
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:20,340
of the towns had easel signs that they just kind of change out the signs for each election.

46
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:26,120
Our town for the primary had none, other than what was around the perimeter of the building.

47
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,080
We didn't have any signs at all.

48
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:34,120
We have an older community, and not everybody's going to come to the town hall and look the

49
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:39,180
day of the election to see that, you know, the day after our holiday, which is when the

50
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,120
primary was, it was the day after the holiday.

51
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:47,280
Concern that this is affecting our town elections.

52
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:52,300
There's a lot of people, and I can say this personally because we did some campaigning in

53
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,220
2023.

54
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:59,880
We were down at the transfer station, and we'd go up to cars, and it was during the time

55
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:03,720
that they were going to change the property lines.

56
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:10,360
And we would go up to people that were going to the transfer station and talk to them about

57
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,360
what was up and coming.

58
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:17,480
And what surprised me the most about this is how many people had no idea that we had a

59
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,020
town election.

60
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:20,580
And they were like, is it November?

61
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,800
Like, people just don't know.

62
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,980
And I think it's harming our budget.

63
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,460
Like, I think we're, what are we, on the fourth year now where it hasn't passed?

64
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:31,440
So I feel like we really need to do something about it.

65
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:32,380
Now, not here.

66
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:36,880
I know the sign, this is owned by the Lions Club, and the Republican Committee is already

67
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:37,280
on that.

68
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:40,980
But for the town, I mean, the primary, there should be signs out.

69
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:45,420
For the town election, how about we had, we have a sign at the transfer station.

70
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:49,540
I know Hampstead, because I work in that area, there are signs everywhere.

71
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,680
They had easel signs, which they took down.

72
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:55,020
But for the primary, I saw at least four throughout the town.

73
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:57,520
And I saw it in other towns, too, everywhere.

74
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,680
So I do think it's something we need to work on.

75
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:03,120
I'd love to see our budget pass.

76
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:08,080
And I don't, I think if we just keep getting the same voters and people aren't educated

77
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:12,140
and are unaware that there's a March election, nothing's going to change.

78
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,220
And I think our town is hurting.

79
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:17,900
We need the funds, and we need people to come out and vote.

80
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:23,700
But I truly believe after what I witnessed in 2023 with talking to voters, they just,

81
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:28,380
they're unaware that there's a March election, so many of them, which really surprised me.

82
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,960
I know I'm very passionate about elections.

83
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,400
I just thought everybody knew about it.

84
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,100
So that's my comment.

85
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:41,320
It has been really sad that we've missed a lot of, with not having really the Tri-Town Times,

86
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:48,300
I feel like you miss that one grouping of individuals where we were reported all the time.

87
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:52,220
Every week somebody was here at a meeting and then reporting on Sandown and Sandown's business.

88
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,080
And we just don't have that anymore.

89
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:56,940
And a lot aren't on necessarily Facebook.

90
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:57,980
We put it on Facebook.

91
00:04:58,180 --> 00:04:59,800
We put it all over the website.

92
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,000
We obviously post here.

93
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:05,740
It's constantly talked about for months prior to, but if you're not involved in the process,

94
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:07,300
you may not necessarily know.

95
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,840
I can say I'm personally not on Facebook.

96
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:12,220
There's a lot of people that have chosen not to be on.

97
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,260
So again, there's a group of scenes.

98
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:15,560
But who reads the newspaper, too?

99
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:21,660
You know, it's kind of what is, there is, you know, really not being utilized as much as it used to be.

100
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:23,140
Yeah, you would be shocked.

101
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:27,480
If we went up to 10 cars, I'd say two people know about the March election.

102
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:28,760
And I was just blown away.

103
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,460
I'm like, why do people not know about this?

104
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:32,040
Everybody thought it was November.

105
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:36,520
So I would just like to see, again, it's just my opinion.

106
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:39,020
It seems like we need to pass a budget.

107
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:41,620
So people need to know about the town election.

108
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:43,940
Hey, Eddie.

109
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:46,060
Mrs. Brown, it's 100% right.

110
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,360
I mean, it's been going on for a long time.

111
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:53,560
And it's gotten worse because they just don't know.

112
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,080
And it's a great idea.

113
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,020
I did see some, I think it was Brentwood.

114
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:57,940
Yeah.

115
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:00,440
Who paid for the signs, I don't know.

116
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:03,040
But, you know, vote in town election.

117
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:05,240
And Epping, I think, put some up, too.

118
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,420
Well, I called me.

119
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,220
You're talking about signs.

120
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:08,180
What kind of signs?

121
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:11,060
Are they doing the big light up, you know, generator signs?

122
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,300
Those are the bigger towns, like Exeter.

123
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,180
Because I know I was over in there in McFarland.

124
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:21,040
They had a huge easel that, not easel, like lighted sign, digital sign.

125
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:21,320
Yeah.

126
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:24,220
That was, I saw at least two of them there.

127
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:32,180
Hampstead, in the town that I work in, the area that I work in, on our property, they did an easel sign.

128
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:33,680
The town did, because I did call.

129
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,460
I was like, maybe I could do some work on this.

130
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:36,480
I just ran out of time.

131
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:38,420
But I did walk up to them.

132
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,840
And what I noticed is it's like an easel sign.

133
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,780
And then it looks like just like a weatherproof piece of paper.

134
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,300
And they just change it, which I love.

135
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,220
Because you just invest in the signs.

136
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:52,740
And then you just, you know, just replace it for every election.

137
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:54,240
They did have them everywhere.

138
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,960
They were, you know, on our property.

139
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,940
As I drove around, I'm like, we need them.

140
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:03,720
I mean, I don't know how expensive a digital sign was.

141
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,080
But I definitely, I did complain to Tom.

142
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,780
I'm like, we've got to do a better job here.

143
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:08,980
We've got to get people out to vote.

144
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,260
And I think people will come out.

145
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:11,860
I do.

146
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,280
If they know about it.

147
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:15,480
So thank you.

148
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:16,760
Valid point.

149
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:17,640
Okay.

150
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:18,620
No, it is a valid point.

151
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:20,680
Well, that's it.

152
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,400
That's my only comment.

153
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:22,480
Thank you.

154
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,880
Thank you all for what you're doing.

155
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:24,500
Appreciate it.

156
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:25,300
Thank you.

157
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:26,300
Thank you for coming.

158
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:26,840
Thanks, Linda.

159
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,540
Excuse me.

160
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:30,260
Erica.

161
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:37,280
Hi.

162
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:41,420
Erica Olsen here for the Oktoberfest committee.

163
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:49,700
It's right around the corner, October 17th, 12 to 10 at Sandlots down below.

164
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:53,160
We have bands.

165
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:58,920
Some of the bands this year are the Oberlander Hofro band.

166
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:05,180
That was the original Oktoberfest band back in the 70s.

167
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:10,040
There's Hot Pasta, Stumpy Joe Band, and more.

168
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:16,860
There is a beer tent sponsored by the Lou Festo.

169
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:17,020
Yeah.

170
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,740
The Lou Festo committee.

171
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:19,260
To the Lou.

172
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:19,340
To the Lou.

173
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:19,680
Yeah.

174
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,160
Committee.

175
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:26,180
So there's German beer, seltzer, and wine.

176
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,440
We have food trucks.

177
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:31,120
We have 50-plus craft vendors come in this year.

178
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:38,000
The bug club will be rolling in around 2 o'clock, so don't miss that.

179
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,840
We have scavenger hunt going for kids.

180
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:48,600
Fry, pee, and toss for adults, well, women and kids.

181
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:56,680
There's lots more games, so follow us on Facebook for the schedule.

182
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:07,460
There's no pets allowed on the property, so just please keep your pets home.

183
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:15,400
We do have a bonfire, hopefully, if the weather stays like this.

184
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,980
A little bit of rain here, but none on our day.

185
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:22,540
So it's October 17th from 12 to 10 at Sandlots.

186
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:26,820
We also are doing raffle tickets for cornhole boards.

187
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:38,520
So the committee will be at Triple Elm on Wednesday, quarter of four, selling them until dark time.

188
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:41,320
So they're five for one or five for $20.

189
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,440
So hope to see everybody there.

190
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:45,760
Thank you.

191
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:46,940
Thank you.

192
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,480
What's the frying pan toss?

193
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:50,500
Is that like husband and wife's?

194
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:51,080
No.

195
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:53,440
It's the woman's frying pan toss.

196
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:57,400
They take the cast-iron frying pan and toss it and see how far they can go.

197
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:58,980
Oh, I've never seen that.

198
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,840
They're looking for husbands to volunteer as the targets.

199
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:01,400
Are you interested?

200
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:05,980
No, I just think it's real catchy.

201
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:09,140
Yeah, it's a good event, as you know.

202
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,300
Oh, no, the event's phenomenal.

203
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:13,060
I'm glad you added stuff to it.

204
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:17,560
We have a corn maze coming also, so that's new this year.

205
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:18,540
Nice.

206
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:18,980
Nice.

207
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:19,620
Yeah.

208
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:22,040
See everybody there.

209
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:22,720
Thank you.

210
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:32,760
Okay, moving on to our sixth floor, Tim Robinson, the chairman of Sandow Historical Society.

211
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:38,380
Discussion guns, a grant opportunity for the Train Depot Museum.

212
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:38,900
Yes.

213
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,620
Good evening, everybody.

214
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:46,400
I came before you a couple months ago just giving you an update where we are with the Historical Society.

215
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:53,840
We're now in the process of contracting with a company called Bedard Historic Preservation and Restoration.

216
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:54,980
We're up in Gilmanton.

217
00:10:54,980 --> 00:11:00,600
And Steve Bedard has over 50 years of experience doing building assessments.

218
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:06,220
And so he's going to work with us this fall to do a detailed building assessment.

219
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:13,900
In that, there will be a program plan of what it will take to rent it for any building to restore it back to its original properties.

220
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:17,320
There will be a timeline and a budget estimate.

221
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:27,460
With that information, we'll be able to go forward and start writing grants this winter to try to start receiving some funds to know to start doing the work.

222
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:33,140
Right now, the proposal to do the building assessment is about $6,000.

223
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:37,640
So it's a little more expensive than I'd like, but it's very detailed.

224
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:45,260
And what he's going to do is help write the grant to get a 50% support of that.

225
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:48,060
So the New Hampshire Preservation Alliance is on board with us.

226
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:49,600
I've talked to him several times.

227
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,860
He's written many grants for the Preservation Alliance.

228
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:57,600
So we feel pretty confident that we'll be able to get a $3,000 matching grant.

229
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,820
So that will require the Historical Society to come up with $3,000.

230
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:05,580
Right now, we need to come up with $1,500 for a down deposit.

231
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:10,220
We have about $2,500 in our fund right now.

232
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:17,180
I'm a little concerned about the cost of heating oil this winter and what that's going to impact to our budget.

233
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:21,400
But we are actively selling ornaments throughout the fall here.

234
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:23,480
We're going to be at the old Oktoberfest.

235
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:26,360
We have a paranormal event coming up.

236
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:31,960
And we'll be at the town vote, the election, selling those ornaments also.

237
00:12:33,180 --> 00:12:39,500
But if anything we can do, if the town has any ability to help offset some of these costs,

238
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:42,080
it'd go a long way to help the Historical Society.

239
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:44,740
So I know there's nothing budgeted at the moment.

240
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,820
But just letting you know, this is where we are.

241
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:47,900
We're moving forward.

242
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:50,980
We are going to pull the trigger on this $1,500 to get this going.

243
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:55,620
Because I'd like to have engineering assessment done this fall so we can start writing the grants in the winter.

244
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:56,740
Okay.

245
00:12:57,460 --> 00:12:57,780
Nice.

246
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,440
So I have a lot of information I can provide you.

247
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:10,980
