730
00:35:21,080 --> 00:35:22,380
Does that $45,000 stay in there?

731
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:22,680
Yes.

732
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:29,860
So in reality, what you should do when you're creating the default budget for, not for 27,

733
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:32,720
because 27, it's already in there.

734
00:35:32,940 --> 00:35:33,160
Yeah.

735
00:35:33,420 --> 00:35:35,200
And we need it for this year so you would keep it.

736
00:35:35,220 --> 00:35:36,580
But I'm talking for 28.

737
00:35:37,220 --> 00:35:41,760
If 28's budget were to fail or when you're developing the default budget for 28,

738
00:35:42,980 --> 00:35:49,280
the legal terminology is the prior year's budget plus or minus any contractual obligations

739
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:51,540
or one-time expenditures.

740
00:35:51,540 --> 00:35:57,820
If you know that you're not supposed to have it any longer, you're supposed to remove it.

741
00:35:58,940 --> 00:35:59,380
Oh.

742
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:00,880
That's what I was curious.

743
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:03,500
If you know it's an expenditure that you don't need.

744
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:05,480
Similar to a revaluation.

745
