1550
01:07:47,260 --> 01:07:52,940
We're going to be reviewing the proposed lease renewal for the postage machine and holding machine.

1551
01:07:52,940 --> 01:07:57,280
So we were contacted a while ago.

1552
01:07:57,400 --> 01:08:05,080
Our existing lease that we have today on our – I just want to make sure.

1553
01:08:05,180 --> 01:08:05,320
Yeah.

1554
01:08:05,380 --> 01:08:06,180
I'm on the mailing sheets.

1555
01:08:06,280 --> 01:08:11,720
So the existing lease that stands today is expiring on January of 27.

1556
01:08:12,360 --> 01:08:15,280
Right now we're paying $158.88 a month.

1557
01:08:15,640 --> 01:08:22,920
Once the lease ends, it rolls into an evergreen, which is apparently their version of what they call a month-to-month billing.

1558
01:08:22,940 --> 01:08:24,240
At that point.

1559
01:08:25,080 --> 01:08:38,180
And because obviously as the machine ages, the servicing needs increase, and that rate steps up about $23 more a month for a total of about $182.08 per month on the same aging equipment.

1560
01:08:38,180 --> 01:08:52,260
They're offering kind of an early renewal if you want, a few months early, to give us a comparable new version of the current model that we already have with basically continuing paying lease payments that we're already paying,

1561
01:08:52,320 --> 01:08:58,080
and we'll have to continue to pay after the fact, which come up to $166.24 a month.

1562
01:08:58,080 --> 01:09:00,640
So smaller – much smaller increase.

1563
01:09:02,300 --> 01:09:04,200
They're calling it a why-wait program.

1564
01:09:04,400 --> 01:09:12,680
It's just something that they've – typical copier and, you know, these companies often do these early renewal programs.

1565
01:09:12,680 --> 01:09:18,420
Yeah, they want to get everybody done the contract by throwing the big carrot out there and saying, hey, this is what your payment's going to be.

1566
01:09:18,780 --> 01:09:20,840
But if you do it now, you can pay this little carrot.

1567
01:09:21,220 --> 01:09:23,660
Do we get a discount on postage through them?

1568
01:09:23,820 --> 01:09:24,180
Yes.

1569
01:09:24,760 --> 01:09:25,940
Yes, we do.

1570
01:09:27,120 --> 01:09:27,340
Yeah.

1571
01:09:27,340 --> 01:09:34,000
So, I mean, we've had at least payment on a mailing machine since I've worked here for the last 20 years.

1572
01:09:34,200 --> 01:09:35,680
You know, it basically does the –

1573
01:09:35,680 --> 01:09:40,460
I remember when we set aside the splurge and get the folding just to save on the amount of labor hours.

1574
01:09:40,460 --> 01:09:48,020
And it has saved massive amounts of time in that office to be able to have that machine that not only folds but stuffs the envelope as well.

1575
01:09:48,200 --> 01:09:50,720
So it's a huge savings to us.

1576
01:09:51,020 --> 01:09:56,440
Do they replace that machine at all during the – it's tenure or is it just for servicing?

1577
01:09:58,100 --> 01:09:59,420
This machine is brand new.

1578
01:09:59,500 --> 01:10:00,480
It's a brand new machine.

1579
01:10:00,660 --> 01:10:05,040
The one that's down there right now was new five years ago.

1580
01:10:05,160 --> 01:10:05,500
Okay.

1581
01:10:05,540 --> 01:10:06,220
Almost five years ago.

1582
01:10:06,240 --> 01:10:07,280
So they're going to replace it then?

1583
01:10:07,440 --> 01:10:07,800
Yes.

1584
01:10:08,000 --> 01:10:08,200
Okay.

1585
01:10:08,800 --> 01:10:09,140
Yes.

1586
01:10:09,780 --> 01:10:10,040
Yep.

1587
01:10:10,580 --> 01:10:14,580
And basically it's a comparable new version of the current model that we already have.

1588
01:10:15,000 --> 01:10:15,480
Okay.

1589
01:10:16,720 --> 01:10:19,880
So Tanya wanted me to present this and just bring it up.

1590
01:10:20,460 --> 01:10:22,000
Technically, it is in her office.

1591
