1680
01:14:10,460 --> 01:14:10,800
Perfect.

1681
01:14:10,880 --> 01:14:11,380
At the end of the month.

1682
01:14:12,220 --> 01:14:12,920
Very nice.

1683
01:14:14,200 --> 01:14:14,600
Awesome.

1684
01:14:15,200 --> 01:14:15,540
Okay.

1685
01:14:15,860 --> 01:14:17,360
Old business, Lynn, I see.

1686
01:14:20,360 --> 01:14:21,760
I just saw something, yeah.

1687
01:14:22,000 --> 01:14:23,560
I don't have anything for old business.

1688
01:14:23,760 --> 01:14:24,180
Oh, good.

1689
01:14:25,180 --> 01:14:26,220
I see correspondence.

1690
01:14:26,220 --> 01:14:30,720
We had Dragon with our early fall update.

1691
01:14:30,720 --> 01:14:32,960
I saw that.

1692
01:14:33,500 --> 01:14:34,340
Dragon Mosquito.

1693
01:14:34,840 --> 01:14:35,020
Yep.

1694
01:14:35,080 --> 01:14:39,900
Dragon Mosquito gave our early fall update, basically letting us know the status of some of the local areas.

1695
01:14:39,900 --> 01:14:54,020
Thankfully, we have been, oh God, knock on wood, we've been okay so far and haven't had anything show up as far as West Nile, AAA, or the Jamestown Canyon, I think it's shown up as a couple locations as well.

1696
01:14:54,020 --> 01:14:55,440
But we're good.

1697
01:14:55,520 --> 01:14:56,540
We're doing well with that.

1698
01:14:56,740 --> 01:15:01,460
If anyone's interested to seeing the full report, it is posted on the health department page.

1699
01:15:03,020 --> 01:15:03,500
I see.

1700
01:15:03,620 --> 01:15:15,020
The planning commission has sent me a nice letter saying, hey, they're requesting dues from us for the upcoming year of $7,703.

1701
01:15:15,740 --> 01:15:20,280
This is calculated based on the 25 Office of Planning and Development population.

1702
01:15:20,420 --> 01:15:26,520
Estimate of standout of 6,757 people at a rate of $1.14 per capita.

1703
01:15:26,780 --> 01:15:28,020
When they raised it, it used to be a buck.

1704
01:15:28,020 --> 01:15:29,080
They raised it up from $1.

1705
01:15:29,440 --> 01:15:30,280
Yeah, it used to be a buck.

1706
01:15:30,500 --> 01:15:31,360
Now it's $1.14.

1707
01:15:31,480 --> 01:15:31,920
They went up.

1708
01:15:32,320 --> 01:15:33,620
Why don't we negotiate that?

1709
01:15:35,400 --> 01:15:35,800
So.

1710
01:15:40,580 --> 01:15:42,540
I don't know we had three default budgets.

1711
01:15:43,120 --> 01:15:44,360
Let's be realistic.

1712
01:15:45,480 --> 01:15:48,800
Well, we can put a note into them and say, hey, we're under default.

1713
01:15:49,140 --> 01:15:49,400
Right.

1714
01:15:49,600 --> 01:15:50,300
Three times.

1715
01:15:50,520 --> 01:15:50,740
Right.

1716
01:15:52,580 --> 01:15:53,380
What do they do?

1717
01:15:54,160 --> 01:15:55,160
Otherwise, we might be.

1718
01:15:55,160 --> 01:15:59,160
They help us with all planning issues.

1719
01:16:01,800 --> 01:16:03,400
So they can blacklist us?

1720
01:16:03,520 --> 01:16:03,660
Yeah.

1721
01:16:04,040 --> 01:16:05,760
No, they don't blacklist you, no.

1722
01:16:06,460 --> 01:16:07,540
No, they want our money.

1723
01:16:08,500 --> 01:16:13,380
But they do assist us in doing our, what's it?

1724
01:16:13,380 --> 01:16:15,400
Oh, my God.

1725
01:16:15,500 --> 01:16:16,360
I'm going to brain death.

1726
01:16:16,380 --> 01:16:16,720
Which one?

1727
01:16:18,140 --> 01:16:18,980
Oh, every 10 years?

1728
01:16:19,160 --> 01:16:20,320
Every 10 years, our planning.

1729
01:16:20,780 --> 01:16:22,120
No, it's every 10 years.

1730
01:16:22,540 --> 01:16:23,200
So, yeah.

1731
01:16:23,500 --> 01:16:24,620
We're probably right on target.

1732
01:16:24,620 --> 01:16:26,740
They assist us with numerous plans.

1733
01:16:26,940 --> 01:16:30,260
They have, like, right now, we're working with them with our hazardous mitigation plan.

1734
01:16:30,260 --> 01:16:38,020
They, we have hired them, if you will, to work with us on a grant opportunity through Homeland Security to update our hazardous mitigation plan.

1735
01:16:38,140 --> 01:16:41,860
They help us with various aspects of the planning board.

1736
01:16:41,860 --> 01:16:45,880
We may have stormwater regulations, so a lot, they help us to rewrite our regulations.

1737
01:16:46,400 --> 01:16:48,800
They help conservation in a few different ways.

1738
01:16:48,940 --> 01:16:57,860
It's mostly planning, but they're just resources that we can go to if we need mapping services done in specific ways.

1739
01:16:57,860 --> 01:17:07,040
You know, if we had, like, a housing needs assessment that we needed to do, they can help review our site plans, you know, that are being submitted to towns as well.

1740
01:17:07,360 --> 01:17:13,080
This dues offsets any pricing we would have to pay them, or are we paying them on top of?

1741
01:17:13,620 --> 01:17:16,040
No, we don't pay them on top that I know of.

1742
01:17:16,040 --> 01:17:21,540
We do, but typically we receive grant funds for any of the money that we have to pay for some.

1743
01:17:21,600 --> 01:17:25,380
So, for the hazardous mitigation plan, it's $7,400 for us to do that.

1744
01:17:25,780 --> 01:17:27,220
A portion of that is being paid.

1745
01:17:27,340 --> 01:17:28,860
Our portion is $2,400.

1746
01:17:29,740 --> 01:17:33,080
The rest of it is being paid by a federal, the federal grant.

1747
01:17:33,800 --> 01:17:43,280
Our payment can be in-kind services, so the hours that we're providing to partake in the planning process can be included as far as that requirement to pay $2,400.

1748
01:17:43,280 --> 01:17:50,580
So, they're being, we're going to pay it, but we're being reimbursed from the grant funds to do that.

1749
01:17:50,740 --> 01:17:54,500
That is above and beyond this dues that they're requesting.

1750
01:17:55,420 --> 01:18:01,500
And if we didn't pay these dues, would we not, they would not work with us?

1751
01:18:01,720 --> 01:18:02,040
Is that?

1752
01:18:02,720 --> 01:18:04,180
They may bill us accordingly.

1753
01:18:04,340 --> 01:18:07,340
We may be billed, I don't know, I've actually never asked them that.

1754
01:18:07,540 --> 01:18:09,620
We could be billed accordingly per project.

1755
01:18:09,620 --> 01:18:14,840
But, you know, for any time they do a site plan review, they may just charge us for that instead, individual review.

1756
01:18:15,100 --> 01:18:18,840
If they need to come in and rewrite a regulation for us, they'll just charge us.

1757
01:18:19,040 --> 01:18:22,240
I would think potentially for that specific service.

1758
01:18:23,980 --> 01:18:27,380
And we use them a lot, so it probably makes sense.

1759
01:18:27,380 --> 01:18:32,160
I can't speak specifically on how many times they're called.

1760
01:18:32,300 --> 01:18:38,540
I know in the past, I have definitely seen a representative at many of the meetings when they're in the process of rewriting regulations.

1761
01:18:39,200 --> 01:18:43,560
Typically, one of the representatives are at each of the meetings until that process is done.

1762
01:18:43,560 --> 01:18:53,600
They're pretty efficient, it's just, I mean, sometimes we really need them on the planning board because we don't have the expertise.

1763
01:18:56,000 --> 01:19:00,240
And they come through and sometimes they get us some money to offset everything.

1764
01:19:01,700 --> 01:19:02,860
It's a tough call.

1765
01:19:02,860 --> 01:19:08,420
But that's something that we're going to be doing in our budget.

1766
01:19:09,200 --> 01:19:14,940
We don't have to do anything now, just notifying us that that's what's coming to us as part of our budget.

1767
01:19:14,940 --> 01:19:19,980
In the planning board's budget, it's not yours, but every year they address it to the board of Sloughman, which is why you received a copy.

1768
01:19:22,460 --> 01:19:23,600
I was just being nosy.

1769
01:19:24,220 --> 01:19:24,840
No, you're fine.

1770
01:19:24,960 --> 01:19:25,640
Ask them any questions.

1771
01:19:25,880 --> 01:19:27,540
No, you've got to ask.

1772
01:19:28,380 --> 01:19:28,700
Yep.

1773
01:19:29,780 --> 01:19:31,800
The rest of what I have in here is non-public.

1774
01:19:32,180 --> 01:19:32,540
Correct.

1775
01:19:33,520 --> 01:19:37,920
All right, we've got, last thing on our list is department liaisons.

1776
01:19:38,040 --> 01:19:40,120
So, Eddie, you've got anything other than planning board?

1777
01:19:41,360 --> 01:19:41,760
No.

1778
01:19:42,360 --> 01:19:43,900
Just planning board coming up next week.

1779
01:19:44,440 --> 01:19:44,800
Yep.

1780
